# Analytics chart cards

Use this structure for every analytics chart wrapped in `Card` from `@/components/ui/card`.

## Card shell

- Root: `className="border-slate-200 ring-slate-200/80"` (match other analytics cards).
- `CardHeader`: `className="border-b border-border/60"`.
- `CardContent`: `className="pt-4"` (or `pt-6` only if the chart needs extra top breathing room).

## Header hierarchy (required)

1. **Eyebrow** — small uppercase label, not `CardTitle`:
   - `className="text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-muted-foreground uppercase"`
   - Short scope label (e.g. `Spending trends`, `Top categories`).

2. **Title** — human-readable chart name:
   - `CardTitle` with `className="text-lg"` (sentence case; do not reuse the eyebrow’s uppercase muted style on the main title).

3. **Description** — supporting line(s):
   - `CardDescription` for date range (`spendingDateRangeLabel`), one-line explainer, or empty-state guidance.
   - Prefer a single `CardDescription`; append `rangeLabel` inline when present (`{rangeLabel ? ` ${rangeLabel}` : ""}`).

## Toolbar / controls in header

When placing toggles (e.g. day / month / year) next to the title block:

- Wrap title stack in `<div className="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">`.
- First child: `<div>` containing eyebrow + `CardTitle` + `CardDescription`.
- Second child: control cluster (e.g. `inline-flex rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-1` for segmented buttons).

## Empty states

- Same card shell classes as above.
- Same three-level hierarchy: eyebrow → `CardTitle` (e.g. `No data yet`) → `CardDescription` (short reason + what to do).
- Omit `CardContent` if everything fits in the header; otherwise one short `CardContent` line is fine.

## Do not

- Put the uppercase eyebrow text on `CardTitle` with `text-muted-foreground uppercase` as the only title (that belongs on the `<p>` eyebrow).
- Leave `CardTitle` and `CardDescription` as awkward siblings in a flex row without wrapping them in a `<div>` when controls sit beside them.
